<title>USA: Progressive, Owens-Illinois to be added to S&amp;P 500.</title>
<headline>Progressive, Owens-Illinois to be added to S&amp;P 500.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said Progressive Corp and Owens-Illinois Inc will replace McDonnell Douglas Corp and U.S. Bancorp in the S&amp;P 500 Index after the close of trading on August 1.</p>
<p>McDonnell Douglas is merging with S&amp;P 500 component Boeing Co, while U.S. Bancorp is merging with another S&amp;P component First Bank System Inc. Both deals are expected to close on August 1.</p>
<p>Progressive Corp, an underwriter of non-standard auto insurance and other specialty personal insurance products, will be added to the S&amp;P 500 insurance group.</p>
<p>Owens-Illinois, which manufactures glass and plastic containers, closures and labels, will be added the the S&amp;P 500 containers industry group.</p>
<p>Old Republic International Corp will replace Progressive Corp in the MidCap 400 Index, Standard &amp; Poor's said.</p>
</text>
